# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment files
#
#   .env.local    <- YOUR REAL CREDENTIALS GO HERE. Ignored. Never committed.
#   .env.example  <- TRACKED TEMPLATE. Placeholders only. Never a real value.
#
# The two names look alike and it is easy to type credentials into the wrong
# one. If you are pasting a secret, the file must be .env.local.
#
# What lives in .env.local for this project:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APPWRITE_ENDPOINT   regional, e.g. https://fra.cloud.appwrite.io/v1
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APPWRITE_PROJECT    public by design (ships in the browser bundle)
#   NEXT_APPWRITE_KEY               ROOT CREDENTIAL - bypasses every Appwrite
#                                   permission rule. Rotate if it ever leaves
#                                   this file.
#   APPWRITE_*_COLLECTION_ID        chosen by you via "Custom ID" when creating
#   PLAID_CLIENT_ID / PLAID_SECRET  use the SANDBOX secret, not development or
#                                   production - all three look identical
#   DWOLLA_KEY / DWOLLA_SECRET      from dashboard-sandbox.dwolla.com
#   DWOLLA_ENV                      exactly "sandbox" or "production"; any other
#                                   value throws at module load
#
# Anything named NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle and is public.
# Never rename a secret to NEXT_PUBLIC_* to "make it work" on the client.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production
.env.*.local
.env*.local
!.env.example

